  "coverage_notes": [
    "RSA type matchers retain exact strings/scopes/severities. Their old library/stdlib ancestry incorrectly supplied Go/standard-library provenance; RSA support now remains in asymmetric/rsa. Exact trailer exclusions updated. Broad crypto selectors continue to include RSA.",
    "Indexed XOR consolidated with canonical arithmetic matcher; original C/C++ arithmetic remains, PE/ELF/JS source-expression coverage retained. Removed unsupported cipher-loop/obfuscation mapping, not XOR capability. Node payload consumer updated. Expanded matcher accepts equivalent assignment indexes and excludes equality comparisons.",
    "Service control/delete reference set moved intact to service/control, keeping its consumer observation set and notable severity. Removed unsupported stop-only placement and persistence mapping.",
    "Filename mismatch matcher/exclusions preserved; removed misleading non-architecture name because WinRing0x64.sys legitimately differs from WinRing0.sys. All live YAML consumers updated.",
    "New neutral MSR read/write instruction matchers and batch execution coverage. No hostile primitive added to inflate scores.",
    "Existing container hostile detections preserved (three); all extracted members remain at zero hostile/suspicious findings. Standalone launcher coverage cannot defensibly meet 3-5 hostile traits: pool/wallet/process invocation is fully described, but its bytes contain no attack-specific evasion, persistence or staging. Inferring these would invent behavior. Contextual SFX traits supply hostile container coverage."
  ],
